tyrosec Source Review License 1.0
==================================

Licensor: DAI-KOMIO e.K. (tyrosec), Ahrensfelde, Germany – contact: info@tyrosec.com
Software: tyrosecd (agent) and all files in this repository

1. Purpose
----------
The source code of the tyrosec agent is published so that customers and interested parties can review what a program
with far-reaching privileges does on their servers, and verify that the officially published, signed binaries are
built from exactly this source code. Publication is not a grant of general use. This software is not open-source
software.

2. Permitted without separate consent
-------------------------------------
2.1 Review. Any natural or legal person – including a company, e.g. before or during a contract with tyrosec – may
    read, review and analyse the software, have it read, reviewed and analysed for this purpose by commissioned third
    parties (e.g. reviewers, auditors), and compile (build) it in order to compare the resulting binaries with the
    officially published binaries. Binaries built this way may only be used for that comparison and must not be run.
    Security issues found may be reported to the licensor (see SECURITY.md).

2.2 Private use. A natural person may compile, run and modify the software for themselves on devices or servers they
    own or rent themselves – solely for purposes unrelated to any commercial or professional activity.

3. Not permitted without the licensor's prior written consent
--------------------------------------------------------------
Beyond section 2, the following in particular is not permitted:
a) any distribution of the software or of binaries built from it to third parties, modified or unmodified, and making
   modified versions publicly available;
b) any use by or for companies, self-employed persons, freelancers, associations, federations, public authorities or
   other organisations – including for internal purposes – to the extent it goes beyond review under section 2.1, in
   particular running self-built binaries;
c) any use on behalf of third parties, in particular monitoring or managing other people's servers, or offering it as
   a service or as part of a hosting offering;
d) incorporating the software or parts of it into other software or products;
e) using the software or parts of it to train or improve artificial-intelligence models. The licensor expressly
   reserves reproductions for text and data mining (reservation of use under section 44b(3) of the German Copyright
   Act, UrhG);
f) removing or altering copyright, licence or trademark notices.

4. Use under a tyrosec contract
-------------------------------
tyrosec customers deploy the agent using the officially published, signed binaries. The tyrosec terms and conditions
apply to that use; this licence does not extend them.

